   "text": {
    "L1": "Prime factorisation writes a number as a product of prime numbers.",
    "L2": "Start with 90 and split it into any two factors: 9 and 10.",
    "L3": "Nine and ten are composite, so the tree is not finished.",
    "L4": "Split 9 into 3 and 3, and split 10 into 2 and 5.",
    "L5": "Now every leaf is prime, so stop the tree.",
    "L6": "The prime factorisation is 90 = 2 × 3 × 3 × 5. Multiply back to check.",
    "L7": "A different tree can find the primes in another order, but the final primes are the same."
   },
